            "review_title": "Review at Nhà Hàng Trúc Mây Sa Pa",
            "review_text": "Thikshan A\nNew York City, New York106 contributions\n0\nGood lunch option\nDec 2019 • Couples\nA wonderfully situated restaurant in the heart of Sa Pa town. Serves authentic Vietnamese cuisine. Highly recommend their version of the 5 flavored pork brought out on a sizzling platter. The mixed fried rice with chicken was also good. The type of rice used is a half rice(the grain is pretty small or in halves)... also try their seafood soup... if you need to spice it up ask for additional fish sauce which really accentuates the flavor.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten December 7, 2019\ngiaback l\nThank you so much for taking the time to share your experience with us. We’re really happy to know you enjoyed the five-flavored pork, mixed fried rice and seafood soup.\n\nIt’s lovely to hear that you appreciated the local flavors, and thank you as well for sharing your little tip about the fish sauce — we’re sure it will be helpful to other guests too.\n\nWe truly appreciate your recommendation and hope to welcome you back to Sa Pa and to Trúc Mây again soon. Wishing you many more delicious meals along the way!\nRead more\nWritten September 4, 2026\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
